# No Unicode chrome icons (mandatory)

Windows system UI fonts (Segoe etc.) **lack** many symbol glyphs. Unicode
chrome icons (`✎`, `×`, `✕`, `✓`, `❐`, `─`, …) render as **tofu** (empty
boxes / two vertical rectangles). That is an **icon** problem — not a reason
to ban readable proportional fonts for labels and buttons.

Fluent `Button` from `std-widgets.slint` also looks foreign next to Theme
chrome. Prefer `AppButton`.

This has already bitten caption buttons and Projects edit/delete. Do not
reintroduce Unicode icon glyphs or fluent `Button`.

## Icons

- Chrome actions MUST use **Path geometry** (`TerminalRowIcon`, `CaptionButton`,
  or an inline `Path` with a fixed viewbox).
- NEVER put symbol glyphs in `Text { text: "✎" }` / `"×"` / `"✓"` for buttons
  or row actions.

## Text labels and buttons

- Dialog / form actions MUST use **`AppButton`** (`form-dialogs.slint`) or
  another Theme + `TouchArea` control — never `import { Button } from
  "std-widgets.slint"`.
- Chrome text (menus, sidebar, tabs, dialogs, AppButton) uses bundled
  **Noto Sans** (proportional) via Window `default-font-family: "Noto Sans"`
  and `assets/NotoSans-Regular.ttf` / `NotoSans-Bold.ttf` (OFL).
- NEVER force a **mono** face on chrome (`Noto Sans Mono`, Cascadia Mono/Code,
  Consolas, `Theme.ui-font` pointing at mono). Mono is for the viewport
  bitmap only (separate).
- Do **not** set Window `default-font-family` to a mono family.

## Allowed fluent leftovers

- `Palette` / `SpinBox` may remain until a Theme replacement exists.
- Do **not** add new fluent `Button`, `LineEdit`, or Unicode icon `Text`.

## Agent obligations

- After chrome icon/button/font changes: rebuild
  `cargo build --profile release-dev -p noviewlog-slint` (Windows:
  `.\scripts\run-slint-windows.ps1` or MSVC env + same cargo).
- Grep for `text: "✎"`, `text: "×"`, `text: "✓"`, and `Button` from
  `std-widgets` in `crates/noviewlog-slint/ui/` before calling the work done.
- Grep that chrome is not mono: no `default-font-family: "Noto Sans Mono"` /
  Cascadia Mono on Window.
